      "text": "The roots of the equation $z^{1997}-1=0$ are the 1997th roots of unity, denoted as $e^{2\\pi i k/1997}$ for $k=0, 1, 2, ..., 1996.$\nNote that the sum of all 1997th roots of unity is 0, i.e. $\\sum_{k=0}^{1996} e^{\\frac{2\\pi i k}{1997}} = 0.$\nThis means that the sum of all distinct pairs of roots $v, w$ is obtained as $0 - v - w = - (v + w),$ where $v + w$ is the sum of all distinct pairs of roots. Thus, $v + w = - (v + w).$  Solving for $v + w,$ we find $v + w = 0.$\n\nTherefore, $\\left|v+w\\right| = \\boxed{0}.$ The answer is: 0",
